 "script": "Six Flags shut nine roller coasters after a rider died in Georgia. Cobb County police said one person died and several were hurt on Monday. Witnesses said a man fell from the Goliath coaster, but police haven't confirmed it. Goliath is two hundred feet tall and reaches seventy miles an hour. Here's what changes for your park trip. Six Flags closed nine similar coasters at six parks, the AP reported. That includes California, New Jersey and Ontario. The company says the closures are temporary. What would make you trust a coaster again? Tell us below.",
